### Instruction:
Rewrite the following in-place insertion sort algorithm in Java.

### Response:
public class InsertionSort { 
	public static void inplaceInsertionSort(int[] array) { 
		// Iterate over array elements 
		for (int i = 1; i < array.length; i++) { 
			int value = array[i]; 
			int j = i; 
			// Check whether the adjacent element in 
			// left side is greater or not 
			while (j > 0 && array[j - 1] > value) { 
				// shifting the elements 
				array[j] = array[j - 1]; 
				j--; 
			} 
			// moving the element in right side 
			array[j] = value; 
		} 
	} 
	// Driver Code 
	public static void main(String[] args) { 
		int[] arr = { 20, 12, 10, 15, 2 }; 
		inplaceInsertionSort(arr); 
		for (int i : arr) { 
			System.out.print(i + " "); 
		} 

	}

### Instruction:
Design a class in Java to build a Binary Search Tree.

### Response:
public class BST { 

    /* Class containing left and right child of current node and key value*/
    class Node { 
        int key; 
        Node left, right; 

        public Node(int item) { 
            key = item; 
            left = right = null; 
        } 
    } 

    // Root of BST 
    Node root; 

    // Constructor 
    BST() {  
        root = null;  
    } 

    // This method mainly calls insertRec() 
    void insert(int key) { 
       root = insertRec(root, key); 
    } 

    // A recursive function to insert a new key in BST 
    Node insertRec(Node root, int key) { 

        // If the tree is empty, return a new node 
        if (root == null) { 
            root = new Node(key); 
            return root; 
        } 

        // Otherwise, recur down the tree 
        if (key < root.key) 
            root.left = insertRec(root.left, key); 
        else if (key > root.key) 
            root.right = insertRec(root.right, key); 

        // return the (unchanged) node pointer 
        return root; 
    } 

}

### Instruction:
Implement a binary search algorithm with a given input array.

### Input:
arr = [2, 3, 4, 8, 10, 42, 56, 78, 89]

### Response:
// Binary Search Algorithm 

function binarySearch(arr, x) { 

    let start=0, end=arr.length-1; 

    // Iterate while start not meets end 
    while (start<=end) { 

        // Find the mid index 
        let mid=Math.floor((start + end)/2); 

        // If element is present at mid, return True 
        if (arr[mid]===x) return true; 

        // Else look in left or right half accordingly 
        else if (arr[mid] < x)  
             start = mid + 1; 
        else
             end = mid - 1; 
    } 

    return false; 
}

